            <ArticleTitle>C-reactive protein is a bystander of cardiovascular disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2092-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/eurheartj/ehq242</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A large number of studies have evaluated the association of hs-C-reactive protein with atherosclerosis and coronary heart disease (CHD) in mechanistic, genetic, population-based studies, as well as clinical trials. This paper reviews the collective evidence to determine if hs-C-reactive protein is part of the causal pathway of atherosclerosis and CHD or whether it is a bystander.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
